So the spoilers at www.steelypips.org are wrong.  According to
them, the average damage of elven daggers (the best kind) is
3/2, even ordinary arrows gives 3.5/3.5, with elven arrows and
ya even better (but typically, you won't have that many elven
arrows, and even less ya).  The major advantage of daggers is
that you don't have to change weapons to effectively throw
them---if you have enough arrows to not worry about loosing
them, you can just use bow and arrow even at melee range, and
not worry about that.  Daggers also have a to hit bonus, but
once you've got your luck and experience up a bit, both should
be at about 100% chance of hitting, so that doesn't matter
either.  And arrows are a lot lighter than daggers, so you can
carry a lot more, and not run out as quickly.

That supposes equal skill with both.

In favor of daggers is, of course, the fact that you don't have
to change weapons to throw them effectively---unless you're
using bow and arrow at melee range as well, this is an important
point---, and the fact that they don't disappear, even if your
luck is down and they aren't blessed---which will usually be the
case in the early game.

So it depends.

